The MediaWiki ('LMW') at lojban.org seems to imply that what I thought is=
=20
'official Lojban' is outdated, and to promote a slightly different language=
=20
under the provisional name of La Bangu:
=96 http://mw.lojban.org/index.php/Obsolete:_joiku (note the 'obsolete')
=96 http://mw.lojban.org/index.php/Stub:_La_Bangu
=96 http://mw.lojban.org/index.php/Stub:_Is_Lojban_an_auxlang ('Lojban had =
6=20
words for "and" [=85]' =85 it does still, doesn=92t it?)

So, just to get a clear picture:=20

What is the language promoted by the LLG ('official Lojban')?

I *think* it is=20
http://www.lojban.org/publications/reference_grammar/chapter21.html, and=20
the rest of CLL, superseded only by confirmed errata, and Xorlo. So, eg,=20
{lo broda ku joi lo brode} needs the {ku}, and {mi .e do broda} is not=20
equivalent to *{mi je do broda}.

What is the MediaWiki about?

I *thought* it was just a supposedly user-friendlier copy and continuation=
=20
of the TikiWiki. So, while (as a wiki) chaotic, still (as a part of=20
lojban.org) about (the agreed-upon, ie 'official' version of) Lojban. (By=
=20
the way, I do find the MediaWiki easier to use [well, I try to ignore some=
=20
of the scarier add-ons recently installed], and I am thankful to Gleki for=
=20
putting so much work into it.)

If, however, the MediaWiki is about a different (version of the) language,=
=20
then we should perhaps put a big sign somewhere explaining that what=20
follows, however more brilliant than 'official Lojban' it may be, is not=20
the same thing as the language promoted on the rest of lojban.org. Just to=
=20
not confuse the casual reader. (While I have nothing against playing around=
=20
with dialects, variations in grammar and such=97a living language Lojban=20
shall be=97, I find it particularly confusing to call the 'prestige dialect=
'=20
_obsolete_ or _outdated._)

